.TH SCD-MCP 1 "2026-11-10" "SCD Reporting 1.0.0" "SCD Reporting"
.SH NAME
scd\-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for SCD Reporting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scd\-mcp
[\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-summary\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-tools\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-k\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server on standard input and output so that an MCP client
(Claude Code, Claude Desktop, ...) can post and retrieve entries, run reports and generate
summaries. Each MCP tool calls one route of the SCD Reporting token API with your API token, so the
assistant can see and do exactly what that token can. The client starts the server; you do not run
it by hand except to test it.
.PP
The server speaks JSON-RPC 2.0, one message per line, and implements the initialize-handshake
protocol versions 2024\-11\-05, 2025\-03\-26, 2025\-06\-18 and 2025\-11\-25 (a client asking
for any other version is answered with 2025\-11\-25). Diagnostics go to standard error; standard
output carries only protocol messages. Settings are read once at start-up; a missing URL or token
does not stop the server: each tool call then returns an explanatory error.
.SS Tools
.TP
.B scd_whoami
Account, role, group, report scope, export formats.
.TP
.B scd_list_taxonomy
Projects, categories, entry types, groups, lab priorities, tags, with slugs and ids.
.TP
.B scd_list_my_entries
Your own entries, structured and paged.
.TP
.B scd_get_entry
One entry (json, md, txt, csv, xlsx, pdf).
.TP
.B scd_export_my_entries
All of your matching entries in an export format.
.TP
.B scd_create_entry
Post an entry under your name (not offered with \fB\-\-read\-only\fR).
.TP
.B scd_run_report
Reports-page report in any format (reporting role).
.TP
.B scd_count_report
Count of a report's entries (reporting role).
.TP
.B scd_report_summary
AI summary; a paid model call (reporting role; not offered with \fB\-\-no\-summary\fR).
.PP
Binary formats (xlsx, pdf) must be saved with the \fBoutput_path\fR argument; the server refuses
to replace an existing file unless \fBoverwrite\fR is true. Text results over 400000 characters
must also be saved to a file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Do not offer \fBscd_create_entry\fR. Also \fBSCD_MCP_READ_ONLY=1\fR or config \fBmcp_read_only: true\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-summary
Do not offer \fBscd_report_summary\fR. Also \fBSCD_MCP_NO_SUMMARY=1\fR or config \fBmcp_no_summary: true\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-tools
Print the tools that would be offered and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
These override the environment, \fB.env\fR files and the config file.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " FILE
YAML config file. Default: \fB$SCD_CONFIG\fR, else
\fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml\fR. Naming a file that does not exist is an error.
.TP
.BI \-u " URL" "\fR, \fP\-\-url " URL
Server root URL, e.g. \fBhttps://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " TOKEN" "\fR, \fP\-\-token " TOKEN
API token (Profile \(-> API Token). Prefer \fB\-\-token\-file\fR or the config file:
a token on the command line is visible in the process list and shell history.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Read the token from \fIFILE\fR (used only when no token is set by a higher-priority source).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Request timeout in seconds (default 300; AI summaries can take minutes).
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " FILE"
PEM file of CA certificates used to verify the server.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Do not verify the server's TLS certificate. Testing only.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log each request URL and the response status, type and size to standard error.
The token is never logged.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the client version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are resolved per key in this order, highest first:
.IP 1. 4
command-line options;
.IP 2. 4
environment variables;
.IP 3. 4
\fB.env\fR files: \fI./.env\fR, then \fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env\fR (only \fBSCD_*\fR keys are read;
the current directory's file wins);
.IP 4. 4
the YAML config file;
.IP 5. 4
built-in defaults.
.PP
Config file keys are \fBurl\fR, \fBtoken\fR, \fBtoken_file\fR, \fBtimeout\fR, \fBca_bundle\fR,
\fBinsecure\fR and \fBformat\fR. The file is shared with \fBscd\-post\-entry\fR(1).
Example (see \fIconfig/scd\-client.yaml.example\fR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
url: https://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov
token_file: ~/.config/scd\-reporting/token
format: md
timeout: 300
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run \fBscd\-whoami \-\-settings\fR to see each resolved value and where it came from.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCD_URL
Server root URL.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN
API token.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN_FILE
File containing the API token.
.TP
.B SCD_CONFIG
Path of the YAML config file.
.TP
.B SCD_TIMEOUT
Request timeout in seconds.
.TP
.B SCD_CA_BUNDLE
CA certificate bundle.
.TP
.B SCD_INSECURE
\fB1\fR/\fBtrue\fR/\fByes\fR disables TLS verification.
.TP
.B SCD_FORMAT
Default output format of \fBscd\-report\fR(1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The server rejected the request (HTTP 4xx/5xx). The status and the server's message, including
per-field errors, are printed to standard error. 401 means the token is missing, wrong, revoked
or belongs to a deactivated account; 403 means your role does not allow the request.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error (no URL or token, bad option, missing config file, binary output to a
terminal).
.TP
.B 3
The server could not be reached (DNS, connection refused, TLS failure, timeout).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml
Default config file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env
Per-user \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.I ./.env
Per-directory \fB.env\fR file.
.SH NOTES
All tools use only the Python standard library (PyYAML is used for the config file when installed,
otherwise a simple \fBkey: value\fR reader). Python 3.9 or later. On Windows run them through the
interpreter, e.g. \fBpy scripts\\scd\-report \-f md\fR or \fBpy scripts\\scd_client.py report \-f md\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register with Claude Code for every project:
.PP
.nf
.RS
claude mcp add \-\-scope user scd\-reporting \-\- python3 ~/SCD\-Reporting/scripts/scd\-mcp
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read\-only, with settings passed as environment variables:
.PP
.nf
.RS
claude mcp add \-\-scope user scd\-reporting \-e SCD_URL=https://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov \-e SCD_TOKEN_FILE=~/.config/scd\-reporting/token \-\- python3 ~/SCD\-Reporting/scripts/scd\-mcp \-\-read\-only
.RE
.fi
.PP
Check what the server will offer:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-mcp \-\-list\-tools
.RE
.fi
.PP
Claude Desktop (claude_desktop_config.json):
.PP
.nf
.RS
{ "mcpServers": { "scd\-reporting": { "command": "python3",
    "args": ["/Users/YOU/SCD\-Reporting/scripts/scd\-mcp"] } } }
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBscd\-report\fR(1),
\fBscd\-summary\fR(1),
\fBscd\-entries\fR(1),
\fBscd\-entry\fR(1),
\fBscd\-taxonomy\fR(1),
\fBscd\-whoami\fR(1),
\fBscd_client\fR(3),
\fBscd\-post\-entry\fR(1)
.PP
The API reference: \fI/api/\fR on the server and \fIdocs/CLI.md\fR in the repository.
